# Responsive Standards

Follow `docs/responsive.md`, `docs/design-system/final-tokens.md`, and `docs/architecture/final-architecture.md`.

Rules:

- Build mobile-first.
- Validate layouts conceptually at `390px`, `768px`, `1024px`, `1280px`, and `1560px+`.
- Use `Container` for global horizontal alignment.
- Use official breakpoints: `tablet`, `laptop`, `desktop`, `wide`.
- Cards and grids must stack cleanly on mobile.
- Avoid fixed widths without `max-width`, `min()`, `clamp()`, or responsive variants.
- Use `clamp()` only when fluid behavior is intentional.
- Promote repeated responsive `clamp()` values to tokens.
- Decorative media must not cause horizontal overflow.
- CTAs need comfortable tap targets on mobile.
